---
import learning from '../data/learning.json';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Filters from '../components/Filters.astro';
import { cases } from '../data/content.json';
const entries=cases;
const topics=[...new Set(entries.map(item=>item.topic))];
---
<Shell title="Islamic Misinformation Casebook"><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow">Read before repeating</span> <h1 class="editorial">{learning.heading}</h1> <p>Investigate twelve source-reading claims. Open the evidence, choose a careful conclusion, and copy a correction with its references.</p></section><div class="evidence-band"><span>Fixed source-reading exercises</span> <span>No live claim checker</span> <a href="/sources/">How conclusions are bounded <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="bookmarks-note">The claims are constructed reading exercises, not a list of measured viral trends. “Beyond the cited evidence” keeps a conclusion narrower than “false everywhere.”</p><Filters topics={topics}/><div class="collection-tools"><h2 id="entries">Choose a case</h2> <button class="button secondary" id="copy-saved">Copy my list</button></div> <div class="card-grid">{entries.map(item=><><article class="panel activity-card" data-item-id={item.id} data-search={`${item.title} ${item.topic} ${item.claim}`} data-topic={item.topic}><span class="eyebrow">{item.topic}</span> <h2><a data-reading-link={item.id} href={`/case/${item.id}/`}>{item.title}</a></h2> <p>{item.claim}</p> <span class="micro">{'Claim · evidence · conclusion'}</span> <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={`/case/${item.id}/`}>Open case</a> <button class="button secondary" data-save={item.id} aria-pressed="false">Save</button></div></article>{' '}</>)}</div> <div id="empty" class="empty" hidden><h2>Nothing matches</h2> <p>Try fewer words, change a filter, or turn off “Saved only.”</p></div><script>import "../lib/library";</script></Shell>